From 903d8d03b2fea38dfc91d7781f8ade6df118101f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 08:44:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] 294: 292's question with the addressing heuristic removed
 and the ladder unbuilt

The two arms cross without inventing a verb. 292 is the only measurable thing in
the line - pooled held 201 v 141 over six seeds, z +3.24 - and it already has the
property 293 was built for: the value it is graded on is excluded from the ink and
the word sets, so the label cannot be seen. What 293 contributed was two
disciplines 292 fails: a place defined by strings the encoder never touches, and
negatives not readable off their construction.

--address-from anchor makes an address one exact anchor string. No cosine, no tau,
no word-overlap conjunction, and no relation half - the 293 audit found that half
is a function word on this tape (canada|and, december|the), which is also why
rare_nonzero_rate is 0.0. Nothing is approximated where the evidence is decided.

--open-cands uniform draws the three wrong answers instead of building them by
relatedness, and records each one's distance for the report only. 292's mean_phi
read its own construction back as an inverted landscape on every seed; this is the
arm that separates a property of the corpus from a property of the rungs.

One run answers both open questions: whether the +3.24 win survives without the
heuristic, and whether the inversion survives without the ladder. _check294_open
proves the five construction properties offline.

